msgid "Using Kogito to add rule engine capabilities to an application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide demonstrates how your Quarkus application can use Kogito to add "
"DRL files with rules."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Kogito is a next generation business automation toolkit that originates from "
"well known Open Source projects\n"
"Drools (for business rules) and jBPM (for business processes). Kogito aims "
"at providing another approach\n"
"to business automation where the main message is to expose your business "
"knowledge (processes, rules and decisions)\n"
"in a domain specific way."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 11+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid "A working container runtime (Docker or xref:podman.adoc[Podman])"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example, we build a very simple microservice which offers one REST "
"endpoint:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/find-approved`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This endpoint will be automatically generated based on the query inserted in "
"the Rule Unit of the DRL file.\n"
"It's an example of a stateless invocation (also called \"pure function "
"invocation\") in which the execution of our business rules doesn't have any "
"side effects.\n"
"The output value returned is based uniquely on the input provided."
msgstr ""

msgid "Business rule"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A business rule allows to externalise decision logic into reusable pieces "
"that can be easily\n"
"used in declarative way. There are multiple ways of writing rules like https:"
"//drools.org/learn/dmn.html[DMN models],\n"
"decision tables, decision trees, rules, etc. For this example we focus on "
"the rule format backed by DRL\n"
"(Drools Rule Language)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the complete example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `kogito-drl-quickstart` {quickstarts-tree-"
"url}/kogito-quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

